sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2020-xenobots-02> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "For at least one deciliated, cardiac-muscle-powered design, the upright organisms' direction of movement matched that of the in silico design under random perturbations, and inverting the design significantly reduced net displacement both in silico and in vivo.";
    dc:type "experimental-result";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Designed organisms moved as simulated when upright, much less when inverted";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Kriegman S, Blackiston D, Levin M, Bongard J, “A scalable pipeline for designing reconfigurable organisms”, Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America (2020), doi:10.1073/pnas.1910837117; section “Results › Locomotion.”. Scope: Deciliated Xenopus reconfigurable organisms with cardiac tissue, compared with their simulated designs"
}
